## Develop

```sh
appsctl validate .{{if .WithUI}}
ndpreview serve .          # preview ui.json at the Kobo's screen size on 127.0.0.1{{end}}
```

Copy the folder to `/mnt/onboard/.adds/apps/{{.ID}}/` and open the Apps drawer; tap the refresh button in the drawer header to rescan the apps.

## How the app talks to the user

Inside the drawer a script never prints prose. It answers with a JSON signal such as `{"toast":"hello"}` naming a toast declared in `ui.json` (`report` in `lib/common.sh` does this and prints the localized text instead when you run the script from a shell). Longer work runs in the background and the screen follows it through the `state` action. See `docs/guide/developer-guide.md` in the NickelDrawer repository.

## What it touches

Declare this in `app.json` so reviews and `appsctl validate` can hold the code to it:

- **Network:** `"network": false` today. Set `true` if the app talks to the network.
- **Shared folders:** none today. Add `"storage": {"reads": ["pictures"], "writes": ["inbox"]}` with the logical names listed in `docs/spec/app-format.md` (NickelDrawer repository) when the app reads or writes outside its own `data/` folder.
- Its own `data/` folder needs no declaration. Never ship `data/` in a package.

## Translate

English lives in `app.json` and `locales/en.json`. Copy `locales/vi.json` to `locales/<lang>.json` and translate it; keep the `{placeholders}` unchanged.
